// wwe2k14 patch (Session 93, the per-draw storage window): GPUs whose maxStorageBufferRange is below the 512 MiB shared memory
// (an Adreno 720: 128 MiB) got the memory split over 2 or 4 storage buffers read through an OpSwitch / phi in every shader, which
// those drivers draw as vertex garbage. With the window the shared memory is ONE storage buffer binding that is a window of W
// bytes (W = the limit rounded down to a power of two, at most 512 MiB; windows start every W / 4); each draw binds the window
// its vertex fetches / memexport / index loads fall in, and the shaders subtract the window's base (a system constant).
// auto = on when maxStorageBufferRange < 512 MiB; on = forced (a big GPU then windows of 128 MiB, to test it); off = the split.
